  "aboutDataTitle": "Where the data lives",
  "aboutDataBody": "The database, skills, AI-written documents and image attachments all live under this directory. Backing up means copying furnace.db (or using \"Back up data\" above).",
  "aboutDataDirLabel": "Application data directory",
  "aboutNetworkTitle": "Network egress",
  "aboutNetworkBody": "Only two things reach the network on their own: (1) AI requests, sent to the endpoint you configured in AI settings - conversation text and images both go there; (2) fetch_page, which reads public pages with GET only, no cookies, refuses loopback and private addresses, follows at most 5 redirects and caps a body at 2 MiB. A skill's scripts run only if you switch its network permission on, and that switch decides whether the script runs at all - it does not block individual domains.",
  "aboutGapsTitle": "Known gaps",
  "aboutGapsBody": "(1) No DOCX / PDF output - create_document writes .md / .txt only; (2) a skill's networkAllow is a switch, not per-domain enforcement (that would need OS-level egress control); (3) skill scripts run on Windows only, so those tools are absent on Android; (4) the browser bridge (browser_bridge) is not implemented; (5) the cognitive model has only the memory tier and the fast scheduler wired up - the run/1 session protocol, metacognition and rhythm tiers are not (see docs/MINDNET_ROADMAP.md); (6) fetch_page cannot refuse a host whose address fails to resolve (recorded, unfixed).",

